# Ford Model Y two-door saloon, 1932-1937.
#
# The first British-designed Ford for the small-car market, made at Dagenham:
# 3,556 mm long, 1,410 mm wide, 1,676 mm high, 2,286 mm wheelbase; 933 cc
# sidevalve four. Sold as the Ford Eight; about 153,000 built.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Model_Y
#
# Colours: Black, Maroon, Blue and Green are documented Ford colours of the
# period.
#
# Weight: 120 in total (black 50, maroon 30, blue 22, green 18).
#
# Speed 80 km/h; comfort 25/368 (line). Class 1.
# Dates: 1932-1937 with a road tail to about 1955.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-model-y.blend. References:
# citycars/references/ford-model-y/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
